 "Hybrid ADR Mechanism (Med-Arb) | Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "Hybrid ADR Mechanism (Med-Arb)": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "Mediation first, with an automatic fallback to binding arbitration if a settlement isn't reached — the parties get a genuine chance to settle on their own terms, without losing the certainty of a final, binding outcome.": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "Mediation phase": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "The parties attempt to settle through facilitated mediation, as a first step.": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "Automatic escalation": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "If mediation doesn't produce a settlement within the agreed window, the matter converts to arbitration.": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "Arbitration phase": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "Unsettled issues proceed to a binding arbitral award — before the same neutral, or a separate one if the clause says so.": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
 "The mediation phase is conducted under the Mediation Act, {0}, and the arbitration phase under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, {1}. The two-stage structure is set out in the parties' arbitration clause or submission agreement, and in the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure.": "/dispute-resolution/hybrid",
