 "International Dispute Resolution": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "For cross-border disputes involving a foreign party, foreign-seated proceedings, or a foreign award — administered with the choice-of-law, seat, and enforcement questions cross-border matters raise.": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "Seat & governing law": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "The parties' clause (or Adjudix, by default) fixes the seat, the governing law, and the language of proceedings.": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "International panel appointment": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "A neutral is appointed from Adjudix's international panel, with cross-border and multi-jurisdictional experience.": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "Proceedings across time zones": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "Hearings run online or in a neutral venue, scheduled to accommodate the parties' time zones.": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "Award & cross-border enforcement": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "The award or settlement is drafted for recognition and enforcement in the relevant foreign jurisdiction.": "/dispute-resolution/international",
 "India-seated international commercial arbitration is conducted under Part I of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, {0}; enforcement of foreign awards is governed by Part II, which gives effect to the New York Convention, {1}. The Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure applies to the conduct of proceedings in either case.": "/dispute-resolution/international",
