 "Lok Adalat | Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "A statutory forum for compromise settlement under the Legal Services Authorities Act, {0} — distinct from arbitration or mediation in that its jurisdiction and effect come from statute, not from an agreement between the parties.": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Eligible matter identified": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Only compoundable civil disputes and certain pre-litigation matters qualify.": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Reference to Lok Adalat": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "The matter is referred with the consent of both parties.": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Compromise hearing": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "A panel assists both sides toward a mutually acceptable compromise.": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "A settlement has the force of a civil court decree and is final — there is no appeal.": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Legal basis — read this carefully": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Lok Adalat is a statutory mechanism under the Legal Services Authorities Act, {0}, not a contractual one. Adjudix facilitates access to this forum for eligible matters, but does not itself constitute the Lok Adalat — that authority sits with the Legal Services Authorities. An award made in Lok Adalat is final and binding, and no appeal lies against it.": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Only at Adjudix": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Adjudix Lok Adalat": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "An Adjudix Lok Adalat can be convened during any ADR proceeding. For a single day, a new ADR professional is engaged; each party submits its confidential settlement proposal to them, and they act as a conciliator, keeping every proposal secret. That secrecy is what makes an out-of-the-box settlement possible — one neither side would have put on the table in open proceedings.": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Convene an Adjudix Lok Adalat": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Is Lok Adalat the same as arbitration?": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "What kinds of disputes qualify?": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Ready to start a lok adalat case?": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Check Eligibility": "/dispute-resolution/lok-adalat",
 "Mediation | Adjudix Dispute Resolution Institute": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "A neutral mediator facilitates a structured conversation between the parties — the outcome is whatever the parties themselves agree to, not something imposed on them.": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "Request & mediator appointment": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "Either party requests mediation; a mediator is appointed from the panel.": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "Joint & private sessions": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "The mediator meets with both parties together and separately to surface real interests.": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "Settlement": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "If terms are reached, they're recorded in a written settlement agreement.": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "Mediation at Adjudix follows the Mediation Act, {0}, and the Adjudix Code of ADR Procedure. A settlement agreement reached in mediation is enforceable in the same manner as a judgment of a court, once registered as required under the Act.": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "Is mediation binding?": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "What happens if mediation doesn't reach a settlement?": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "What is the Mediation Act, {0}?": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
 "How long can a mediation under the Act take?": "/dispute-resolution/mediation",
